      "page_title": "Docker Architecture and Runtime Chain",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Daemon and Runtime Chain",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The `docker` CLI is a thin ==client== that sends REST calls",
            "It reaches `dockerd` over the socket `/var/run/docker.sock`",
            "`dockerd` hands the container lifecycle to ==containerd==",
            "containerd calls **runc** through a `containerd-shim`",
            "runc creates the container from kernel primitives, then ==exits=="
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "docker CLI",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "dockerd",
                "sub": "REST API",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "containerd",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "text": "shim",
                "sub": "stays alive",
                "ink": "purple"
              },
              {
                "text": "runc",
                "sub": "exits",
                "ink": "red"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Kernel Building Blocks",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Primitive",
            "Controls",
            "Covers"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "{purple:Namespaces}",
              "what it **sees**",
              "pid, net, mnt, uts, ipc, user"
            ],
            [
              "{blue:cgroups}",
              "how much it **uses**",
              "CPU, memory, block IO, pids"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Layers, COW and OCI",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==overlay2== stacks read-only image layers under one writable layer",
            "==Copy-on-write==: a file is copied up only when modified",
            "Reads fall through to the lower layers at no cost",
            "==OCI specs== fix the image format and runtime behaviour",
            "So one image runs on Docker, Podman and containerd"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Container vs VM",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Aspect",
            "Container",
            "VM"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Kernel",
              "{green:shared} host kernel",
              "own guest kernel"
            ],
            [
              "Runs on",
              "container runtime",
              "hypervisor"
            ],
            [
              "What it is",
              "isolated process",
              "whole virtual machine"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Mounting `docker.sock` into a container casually: it is **root** on the host",
            "Believing a container has its own kernel",
            "Expecting runc to stay running beside the container",
            "Treating namespaces as limits: only cgroups cap resources"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Interview Point",
          "items": [
            "Walk through what happens after `docker run`?",
            "Namespaces vs cgroups: what does each do?",
            "Why is docker.sock access equal to root?",
            "How is a container different from a VM?"
          ],
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Key Takeaways",
          "text": "A container is a namespaced, cgroup-limited process on a shared kernel, started via dockerd, containerd and runc."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`docker top` shows the process with its ==host PID==",
            "Inside the container the same process is **PID 1**",
            "The container is just a process the host can see",
            "The socket reply proves the daemon answers any caller"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "docker",
      "subtitle": "Daemon to kernel"
