              "UID and GID mapping"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 4,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. cgroups in Practice",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`--memory` and `--cpus` write limits into the container's cgroup",
            "`docker stats` reads live usage from those same cgroups",
            "Memory over the cap means the ==OOM killer== ends the process",
            "`--pids-limit` stops fork bombs inside one container"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Who Does What",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Component",
            "Job"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "{blue:dockerd}",
              "REST API, images, networks, volumes"
            ],
            [
              "{green:containerd}",
              "container lifecycle, image pulls"
            ],
            [
              "{purple:shim}",
              "keeps stdio, reports exit code"
            ],
            [
              "{red:runc}",
              "creates the container, then exits"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 3,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Peek at the Writable Layer",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker exec w touch /tmp/x",
            "docker diff w",
            "# A = added, C = changed",
            "docker inspect -f \\",
            "  '{{.State.Pid}}' w"
          ],
          "note": "diff lists writable layer only"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`docker diff` shows files copied up or created by the container",
            "The image layers underneath are never modified",
            "Delete the container and its writable layer is **gone**",
            "`State.Pid` is the same ==host PID== that `docker top` shows"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. OCI Specs",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The ==image spec== fixes layers and config JSON format",
            "The ==runtime spec== defines how runc starts a container",
            "Standard formats keep images portable across tools",
            "Docker, Podman and containerd all run the same image"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Interview Point",
          "items": [
            "Which component actually creates the container?",
            "What does the shim do after runc exits?",
            "What does copy-on-write copy, and when?",
            "Why do OCI specs matter for portability?"
          ],
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Remember",
          "text": "Namespaces hide things, cgroups cap things. Isolation needs both, plus a locked-down socket."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "docker",
      "subtitle": "Daemon to kernel"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Images and Containers",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Image vs Container",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "An ==image== is immutable: read-only layers plus a config JSON",
            "A ==container== is a running instance of that image",
            "One image can start many containers at once"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Names, Tags, Digests",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Name format: `registry/namespace/repo:tag`",
            "Example: `ghcr.io/acme/api:1.4.2`",
            "Tags are **mutable** pointers; retagging moves them",
            "`@sha256:...` digest pins exact content and is immutable"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Lifecycle and docker run",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "created",
                "sub": "docker create"
              },
              {
                "text": "running",
                "sub": "docker start"
              },
              {
                "text": "paused"
              },
              {
                "text": "exited",
                "sub": "stop / kill"
              },
              {
                "text": "dead"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`docker rm` deletes a container that is not running",
            "`docker run` = ==pull if missing== + create + start",
            "`-d` detached, `-it` interactive TTY, `--rm` auto-remove",
            "`--name` names it, `-p 8080:80` publishes, `-e K=V` sets env"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Stop, Kill, Exec, Attach",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Command",
            "Signal",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "stop",
              "SIGTERM, then SIGKILL",
              "10s grace"
            ],
            [
              "kill",
              "SIGKILL",
              "immediate"
            ],
            [
              "exec",
              "none",
              "extra process"
            ],
            [
              "attach",
              "none",
              "PID 1 streams"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Manage, Restart, Limit",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`docker ps -a` lists stopped containers too",
            "`docker images` lists local images; `docker image prune` drops dangling ones",
            "Restart policies: `no`, `on-failure[:max]`, `always`, `unless-stopped`",
            "`--memory` and `--cpus` cap resources",
            "Over the memory cap: OOM-killed, exit code **137**"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker run -d --name api \\",
            "  -p 8080:80 -e MODE=prod \\",
            "  --memory 256m --cpus 0.5 \\",
            "  --restart unless-stopped \\",
            "  nginx:1.27.0"
          ],
          "note": "over 256m means OOM kill, exit 137"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Depending on `:latest`: builds become **non-reproducible**",
            "Storing data in the writable layer: lost on `docker rm`",
            "Fix: pin a tag or digest, keep data outside the container"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Interview Point",
          "items": [
            "Why is a tag mutable but a digest not?",
            "What does docker run do step by step?",
            "stop vs kill: which signals, what grace?",
            "Exit code 137: what happened?"
          ],
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Key Takeaways",
          "text": "Images are immutable layers, containers are disposable instances: pin digests, expect data loss on rm."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "docker",
      "subtitle": "Layers, lifecycle, run flags"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Dockerfile and Build Optimization",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Core Instructions",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`FROM` picks the base; `WORKDIR` sets the working directory",
            "`RUN`, `COPY`, `ADD` change the filesystem at build time",
            "`ENV` persists at runtime; `ARG` exists only during build",
            "`EXPOSE` documents a port; `USER` drops root",
            "`ENTRYPOINT` and `CMD` define what the container runs"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Layers and the Cache",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Each ==RUN==, ==COPY== and ==ADD== creates one layer",
            "Chain related commands with `&&` to keep layers few",
            "A changed instruction **invalidates** every instruction after it"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "FROM node",
                "sub": "cached"
              },
              {
                "text": "COPY manifest",
                "sub": "cached"
              },
              {
                "text": "RUN npm ci",
                "sub": "cached"
              },
              {
                "text": "COPY src",
                "sub": "edit here"
              },
              {
                "text": "RUN build",
                "sub": "reruns"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Cache-Friendly Order",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "FROM node:22-slim AS build",
            "WORKDIR /app",
            "COPY package*.json ./",
            "RUN npm ci",
            "COPY . .",
            "RUN npm run build"
          ],
          "note": "manifests first, source last"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Pick the Right Form",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Pair",
            "Prefer",
            "Why"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "COPY vs ADD",
              "COPY",
              "ADD untars, fetches URLs"
            ],
            [
              "ENTRYPOINT vs CMD",
              "Both",
              "exe fixed, CMD = default args"
            ],
            [
              "Exec vs shell form",
              "Exec",
              "shell form eats SIGTERM"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 2,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Small and Fast Builds",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Multi-stage: `FROM node AS build`, then `COPY --from=build` into a slim stage",
            "The final stage drops compilers and toolchains",
            "Bases: ==alpine==, ==distroless==, ==slim==, or `scratch` for static binaries",
            "Alpine uses musl, which can **break** glibc binaries"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "BuildKit runs independent stages in parallel",
            "`--mount=type=cache` keeps npm or apt downloads between builds",
            "`--mount=type=secret` exposes tokens that never land in layers",
            "`.dockerignore` keeps `node_modules`, `.git` and secrets out of context"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`RUN apt-get update` alone gets cached **stale**",
            "Fix: `apt-get update && apt-get install -y x`, then clean `/var/lib/apt/lists`",
            "`CMD node app.js` is shell form: SIGTERM never reaches node",
            "Use `[\"node\",\"app.js\"]` so the app runs as PID 1",
            "`COPY . .` before install busts the dependency cache"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Key Takeaways",
          "text": "Order for the cache, use exec form, and ship a slim multi-stage image."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Shell form wraps the command in `/bin/sh -c`",
            "`docker stop` signals sh, which **swallows** SIGTERM",
            "Exec form lets the app shut down gracefully"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "docker",
      "subtitle": "Fast, small images"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Multi-Stage Builds, Mounts and Debugging",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Multi-Stage in Practice",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "FROM node:22 AS build",
            "COPY . .",
            "RUN npm ci && npm run build",
            "FROM node:22-slim",
            "COPY --from=build /dist /app",
            "CMD [\"node\",\"/app/main.js\"]"
          ],
          "note": "final image ships only the output"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Check Your Layers",
          "text": "Run `docker history img` to see each layer's size and spot the heavy RUN steps."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Exec vs Shell Form",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "# shell form: sh is PID 1",
            "CMD node app.js",
            "# exec form: node is PID 1",
            "CMD [\"node\",\"app.js\"]"
          ],
          "note": "exec form receives SIGTERM"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. ENTRYPOINT and CMD",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Instruction",
            "Role",
            "`run` args"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "ENTRYPOINT",
              "fixed executable",
              "appended to it"
            ],
            [
              "CMD",
              "default arguments",
              "replace CMD"
            ],
            [
              "Both together",
              "exe + default args",
              "override args only"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 2,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Clean apt-get Layer",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "RUN apt-get update \\",
            " && apt-get install -y curl \\",
            " && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*"
          ],
          "note": "update, install, clean in one RUN"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. BuildKit Mounts",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "RUN --mount=type=cache,\\",
            "    target=/root/.npm \\",
            "    npm ci"
          ],
          "note": "cache stays out of the image"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`--mount=type=secret` exposes a token only during that RUN",
            "Secrets never land in layers or `docker history`",
            "Never pass tokens with `ENV` or `ARG`: both stay visible"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Debug a Failing Build",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker build \\",
            "  --progress=plain \\",
            "  --no-cache -t app ."
          ],
          "note": "shows the exact failing step"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Interview Point",
          "items": [
            "Why copy package.json before the source?",
            "CMD vs ENTRYPOINT: what does docker run args override?",
            "Why does a shell-form CMD ignore docker stop?",
            "How do multi-stage builds shrink an image?"
          ],
          "ink": "purple"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "docker",
      "subtitle": "Fast, small images"
